# Two farms side by side, a crossroads just past them, and a farm on the new
# street close by: it faces another way, and the fields share out the land.
> new empty
> free on
> construction off
> build farm at s0:43
  #1 farm at s0:43-48, done
> build farm next
  #2 farm at s0:49-54, done
> build crossroads at s0:55
  #3 intersection at s0:55-57, done
> expect streets 2
  ok: 2 streets
> streets
  s0  runs east (lots on its north side), cells 16..246
  s1  runs north (lots on its west side), cells 127..135, from crossroads #3
    crossroads #3: s0:56 = s1:131 (cell A56)
> ride #last
  rider: s0:56 facing +
> turn up
  rider: s1:131 facing +
> expect rider s1
  ok: the rider is on s1
# the end of the road is kept for more road: lay some, then build beside it
> lay road 1
  s1 now runs cells 127..162
> ride s1:136
  rider: s1:136 facing +
> build farm here
  #6 farm at s1:136-141, done
> expect at s1:136 farm done
  ok: #6 farm at s1:136-141, done
> expect fields at s0:43 24
  ok: #1 has 24 fields
> expect fields at s1:136 24
  ok: #6 has 24 fields
> list
  #1  farm  s0:43-48  done  fields=24 (grass 24, fallow 0, growing 0, ripe 0)
